  "title": "How the First World War Opened a Chain of Imperial Reconfiguration",
  "summary": "The First World War brought industrial capacity, state mobilization and imperial competition into a new density. Total war expanded the organizational reach of states over population and production, while the end of the conflict pushed several imperial systems into dissolution and succession.",
