  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionCode": "book6-article-005-body",
      "heading": "Reading the Book VI structure",
      "anchor": "article-body",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The First World War brought industrial capacity, state mobilization and imperial competition into a new density. Total war expanded the organizational reach of states over population and production, while the end of the conflict pushed several imperial systems into dissolution and succession."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "These sections focus on how war altered operating structures rather than reducing imperial dissolution to a single cause. Battle, finance, national politics and succession arrangements combined differently across regions."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This article distinguishes historical fact, historical reconstruction and structural interpretation in the manuscript. Later outcomes are not treated as inevitable at the time, and motives or causal claims not present in the manuscript are not added."
        }
      ]
    }
